{
  "format": "konareef-credential-vectors/v2",
  "_comment": "Shared credential-pattern vectors (SECRET-SCAN). internal/pod/credentials_test.go checks the konareef scanner against this file. The reef-core scanner (SECRET-SCAN-R, reef-core#88) reads the same file and must return the same findings and digests. Engine rule: compile each pattern from internal/pod/credentials.go with no UTF and no UCP flag (in Elixir, no `u` modifier) and match over the raw bytes of each line; with UTF or UCP, `\\b` treats non-ASCII letters as word characters and the non-ascii-* vectors fail. Before matching, replace every backslash followed by n, r or t in the line with two spaces. A change here needs a matching change on the other side in a linked MR. No vector holds a whole credential-shaped string: each vector's text is the concatenation of its `parts`, so a secret scanner reading this file sees no key, and a consumer joins the parts in memory. The values are made up and are not credentials. Raw invalid UTF-8 cannot be written in a JSON string, so it has no vector; no pattern uses `.` or a negated class, so a byte that is not ASCII is a non-word byte in both engines.",
  "scanner_version": "v2",
  "classes": [
    "anthropic_api_key",
    "openai_api_key",
    "aws_access_key_id",
    "github_token",
    "gitlab_token",
    "slack_token",
    "private_key_block",
    "jwt"
  ],
